Based on the provided passages, it appears that salary exchange refers to an arrangement where an employee agrees to give up a portion of their salary or bonus in exchange for their employer making a pension contribution. This allows both parties to save money, as the employer pays lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) on the reduced salary, while the employee receives a pension contribution. The calculator provided in passage 1 suggests that this can be a way to set up pension payments that can allow both employers and employees to make a saving. Additionally, passage 3 provides specific details about how the salary exchange works for members of certain pension schemes, including the University Superannuation Scheme (USS), the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USPAS), and the Scottish Universities Superannuation Scheme (SGSS).

